  "id": "86980d58-4683-5b0b-8dbc-cafb327e1049",
  "slug": "south-shore-bar-pizza-recipe-7568213",
  "name": "South Shore Bar Pizza",
  "recipe_type": "snack",
  "brief_description": "South Shore Bar Pizza is the easiest plain cheese pizza you will ever make. It\u2019s thin, with a cracker-like crust, reminiscent of bowling alley, snack bar, or movie theater pizza. This version has a bit of a California edge, with piquant Cheddar and Monterey Jack cheese, rather than plain mozzarella.",
  "cuisine": "Italian American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Stir yeast, sugar, and water together in a bowl; let sit for about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Stir in flour and mix until a dry, shaggy dough forms. Add salt, butter, and 2 tablespoons oil and mix to combine."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Knead with your hands in the bowl until dough comes together, then turn out onto the counter and continue to knead until a stiff but smooth dough forms, about 1 to 2 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Return dough to the bowl; rub the surface of the dough with a small amount of oil. Cover the bowl and let dough rise in a warm place until doubled in size, up to 6 hours. Alternately, place dough in the refrigerator to rise overnight."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Meanwhile, make the pizza sauce. Blend San Marzano tomatoes until smooth using a stick blender or in the jar of an electric blender. Measure out 1 1/2 cups of the tomato puree and place into a bowl. Stir in 1 teaspoon kosher salt, dried oregano, and cayenne pepper. Refrigerate until ready to make the pizzas."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 500 degrees F (260 degrees C). Drizzle 1 1/2 to 2 tablespoons oil into a 10- to 12-inch pizza pan."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Divide dough into 4 pieces and roll into balls. Keep dough covered when not using. Press 1 dough ball into a round disc and place on the prepared pizza pan. Press and stretch dough flat, almost all the way to the edge of the pan. Poke the dough all over with a fork."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Once the dough is properly punctured, top with about 1/3 cup sauce, spreading all the way to the edge of dough. Top the entire surface with 2 ounces each of Cheddar cheese and Monterey Jack cheese."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until cheese is bubbling and bottom of pizza is browned, 10 to 12 minutes. Repeat with remaining ingredients to make 3 more pizzas."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 10,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 30,
